If you receive a defective product and suffer harm, you can bring a product liability action against the product manufacturer, product service provider, or product seller, as applicable. Additionally, you can file a complaint with the District Commission. If the District Commission is satisfied that the goods are defective, it can issue an order directing the opposite party to take one or more of the following actions:
- Remove the defect pointed out by the appropriate laboratory;
- Replace the goods with new goods of a similar description that are free from any defect;
- Return the price or charges paid by you, along with applicable interest;
- Pay an amount awarded as compensation for any loss or injury suffered due to the opposite party's negligence (including punitive damages or product liability compensation);
- Discontinue or not repeat unfair or restrictive trade practices, or withdraw/cease offering hazardous or unsafe goods.
